[thin] The internal webs meet the 1.5 mm minimum at both chamfered faces: drain-to-ribbon 1.5625 mm and flavor-to-drain 2.7014 mm. The current native face-distance and stock-passage readings are in integration-check.json. The soda bore retains the A fit dimension and the three 4 mm bores use the B drain dimension; black-stock fit and the complete current arrangement are unmeasured.
alternatives: More lateral spread needs more exterior stock or further forward placement. More drain/ribbon separation displaces the row along Y from the steel channel. Smaller bore entrances change the selected fit profile. A joined opening removes independent guidance.
